# macOS cache cleaner

Clears regenerable caches from applications, app containers, Xcode,
Simulators, Homebrew, Quick Look, and current-user temporary storage. It needs
macOS and its system `zsh`. Temporary cleanup defaults to owned files older
than three days; `--all-temp` includes all owned entries.

> **Preview first:** In the TUI, nothing is deleted until the preview finishes
> successfully and you type `CLEAN`. Apply repeats discovery with the same
> settings, so targets may change between the two runs.

## What it can clean

- user and sandboxed application caches
- Xcode DerivedData and Simulator caches
- unavailable Simulator devices
- Homebrew downloads and old package versions
- Quick Look caches and stale current-user temporary files

## Safety

Run it as your normal user, never through `sudo`. It does not target `/System`,
`/Library`, APFS snapshots, swap, backups, documents, Application Support,
Xcode archives, Trash, or live Simulator application data.

Close applications, Xcode, and Simulator before applying the plan.

## Options

| Option | Meaning |
| --- | --- |
| `--all-temp` | include recent current-user temp files |
| `--logs` | include user application and diagnostic logs |
| `--verbose` | print every filesystem target |
| `--apply` | repeat discovery with deletion enabled |
| `--yes` | accept the script's prompt after TUI confirmation |

## Direct CLI

```sh
sys/macos/clean --help
sys/macos/clean --verbose
sys/macos/clean --apply
```

## Exit status

`0` means the preview or cleanup completed without warnings. `1` means input,
platform, privilege, path validation, or one or more cleanup operations failed.
